import Mathlib
import PEqualNP.Defs
import PEqualNP.W951.PureSDR

/-!
# PureSDRWitness: kernel-checked PureSDR certificates

Generated by `one-not/tools/sdrcert/pure_export.py` (Python finds, Lean checks): for each circuit, one
pure option per set (`PureOpt.one Z`: world 1, zero point `Z`; `PureOpt.zero m`: world 0, atom points
`m_u`), checked valid (`PureValid`, by `decide`), its class recomputed in the lift (`pureCls`, union-find
merge set, by `decide`) and equal to a literal in LIFTED wire numbers, the literals pairwise disjoint.
So `PureSDR S gates p` holds on these circuits, with the Lean definitions of `PureSDR.lean`: the
definitions agree with `kill_tests/ext.py` on them. cxT2 and cxe3 are the two hard circuits of
PROOF_PLAN_SUGGESTIONS §0 (2 and 8 pure SDRs there). The other circuits are those of the MergeSDR
certificates (`SDRWitness`, `SDRWitnessFixh16`): CfgI, ADV3, ADV4, ce3, HARD4 (front's and scaffold's),
cxr, scaffold's unique-SDR circuits, cxT4 (n = 15) and the 24 forced-h fixh16 circuits
(`python3 pure_export.py OUT --group fixh16`). Every one has a PureSDR.
-/

